<title>PERU: Peru net international reserves rise to $9.556 bln.</title>
<headline>Peru net international reserves rise to $9.556 bln.</headline>
<dateline>LIMA 1997-06-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Peru's Central Reserve Bank said Monday its net international reserves rose to $9.556 billion by the end of May, up $147 million from the previous month.</p>
<p>Peru's reserves, which have recovered steadily since President Alberto Fujimori's government took power in 1990, ended last year at $8.540 billion.</p>
<p>The government estimates reserves will rise above $10 billion by mid-1998.</p>
<p>((-- Lima Newsroom, 511 221-2134))</p>
